{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/509371-a-generic-merits-question","id":509371,"title":"A generic merits question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-09T18:55:16-07:00","id":509371,"title":"A generic merits question","content":"I was wondering about how other STs handle merits and flaws. In all the games I've played in, the STs allowed players at Character Gen to buy as many merits as they have freebie points as long as they help define the character and make sense. The STs always capped flaws at 7 points. So, any thoughts or comments on how you do it and why. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:31:26-07:00","id":509437,"title":"","content":"To be honest I discourage both. If I have a player who insists then I cap them at 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":".  autocheck changed cap to can 05-09-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T20:14:06-07:00","id":509466,"title":"","content":"My fellow Storytellers from my gaming group and I always ran it the same way as in your games David.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T23:58:28-07:00","id":509662,"title":"","content":"As long as it supports my story or the character concept I do not limit merits or flaws either. It has to be said that if the player has a nice character-idea that inspires me as a ST or simply fits too well, I even don't care about any other character creation limits. &quot;You need way more knowledges but not a single talent for this character? Ok if it sounds like a great concept just go for it. You need X Freebees more to make the concept believable? Take them.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty strict after character creation regarding xp and the use of them. But when you build a new character or even a whole new troupe I adjust the rules as needet to get the best starting situation possible.<br /> <br /> My players even may start elder or methusaleh characters. If they can explain why this character would improve the game and if they can convince me they are able to play the character in question in a believable way ( won't allow elder characters for completely new players for example - usually I recommend all of them to start as a human at least once ao they can learnabout the world of darkness together with their character).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T10:48:51-07:00","id":510007,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies, I've had characters with no merits all the way up to 10 or more depending upon the concept.<br /> <br /> Incbill, do you not like the idea of merits and flaws?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T23:31:47-07:00","id":510467,"title":"","content":"I tend to have players come up with concepts before even looking at the merit/flaw lists. I am not so much afraid of abuse, but sometimes players can get carried away with either or both. I would rather that they have a good handle on their character before they take a gander at some list and decide that they need to be unbondable or have a Dark Fate\u2122.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T23:56:13-07:00","id":510482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/509371-a-generic-merits-question?p=510007#post510007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the replies, I've had characters with no merits all the way up to 10 or more depending upon the concept.<br /> <br /> Incbill, do you not like the idea of merits and flaws?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit back like 15+ years ago now having never used the Merits and Flaws in my games I had a new group in my naivety with them and having no idea how someone could min/max the system I allowed them. I used ten points of both. One player used the system to create a story proof character. This experience has colored my view on Merits and Flaws if players want things now I use an actual story for extra points at character generation. If a player would need a merit for a concept to work then I will allow them to have it. And I then choose the flaws to off set the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:36:50-07:00","id":510561,"title":"","content":"Presumably you allow stuff like Language though, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:57:39-07:00","id":510853,"title":"","content":"When a Merit crosses over with a Background, I usually have them buy the Background instead. Do you really need a &quot;Bar&quot; Merit that can't be dealt with by buying some Resources and Contacts (and maybe Influence). And, if Bar is cheaper, the player should not be getting more bang for his buck using a Freebie for a Merit instead of a Background. I run Merits as being something to get a handle on something that needs a rmechanical reflection that isn't covered by using the rest of the rules. <br /> <br /> Flaws are a different matter, since there aren't any other ways to represent them (aside from Mage's Adversarial Backgrounds... which really work just like Flaws, so same treatment overall). So, since there is no way to get them any other way, I am more apt to let them run as is, with the caveat that the player has to realize that a Flaw is GOING to have negative effects and consequences that they will have to deal with. E.g. If you take Dark Fate, it's not something way out there that you just get to brood about; it WILL happen during the course of the chronicle. If you take a Dark Secret, it WILL come out or you are going to have expend significant effort to keep that from happening. Etc. <br /> <br /> I scrutinize each and every Merit and Flaw purchase just as heavily as every other dot spent vis-a-vis the background the character has outlined and the things they want the character to be able to do (both at character creation and their plan for their character's future development... which plans seldom survive contact with the events of the game wholely intact.&quot;<br /> <br /> I just modify the way the Linguistics Ability works to handle proficiency with additional languages. 6 total languages is not a world-class polyglot, but any means. So I set it up as progressive per dots. So 5 dots is more like 16 languages. And if you take the right Merit, that will go up significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:06:40-07:00","id":511195,"title":"","content":"I personally am not fond of the Mental Flaws, as most of them are personality quirks that should be part and parcel of role-playing one's character correctly rather than something that should be represented by game mechanics for bonus points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}